<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill yield rises to 10.97 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill yield rises to 10.97 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills rose to 10.97 at an auction on June 17 from 10.64 at the previous auction, on June 11, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   June 17	    June 11</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K1809971     KZ43K1109976</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)    500		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	 1,32		 1,55</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)   536		  604</p>
<p> Average price			 97.33 pct	  97.41</p>
<p> Average yield			 10.97		10.64</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Sept 18, 1997     Sept 11, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
